\ Precise gate-index sauce inputs, independent of the full sauce.
\ These quick checks do not run the costly 46-drop pipeline.
\ A signed index is NOT an absolute day. Index -1 must give the
\ pair (Foundation, Foundation-1); index +1 uses Foundation+1.
\ Large-index vectors include 49-digit signed day coordinates.

The sample gate index is a wide signed day.
The sample gate magnitude is a wide quantity.

To check wide gate input counters:
  Put "1" into the sample gate magnitude.
  Set the sample gate index from the sample gate magnitude given -1.
  Prepare wide gate sauce counters given the sample gate index.
  If the wide calendar example's calculation count is not "1",
    put "Wide gate source calculation count failed case 1." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's requested count is not "2",
    put "Wide gate source requested count failed case 1." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day distance is not "2",
    put "Wide gate source distance failed case 1." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day sum is not "3",
    put "Wide gate source sum failed case 1." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day direction is not 1,
    put "Wide gate source direction failed case 1." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1" into the sample gate magnitude.
  Set the sample gate index from the sample gate magnitude given 1.
  Prepare wide gate sauce counters given the sample gate index.
  If the wide calendar example's calculation count is not "1",
    put "Wide gate source calculation count failed case 2." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's requested count is not "3",
    put "Wide gate source requested count failed case 2." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day distance is not "2",
    put "Wide gate source distance failed case 2." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day sum is not "4",
    put "Wide gate source sum failed case 2." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day direction is not 3,
    put "Wide gate source direction failed case 2." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000" into the sample gate magnitude.
  Set the sample gate index from the sample gate magnitude given -1.
  Prepare wide gate sauce counters given the sample gate index.
  If the wide calendar example's calculation count is not "1",
    put "Wide gate source calculation count failed case 3." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's requested count is not "2000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000",
    put "Wide gate source requested count failed case 3." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day distance is not "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000001",
    put "Wide gate source distance failed case 3." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day sum is not "2000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000001",
    put "Wide gate source sum failed case 3." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day direction is not 1,
    put "Wide gate source direction failed case 3." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000" into the sample gate magnitude.
  Set the sample gate index from the sample gate magnitude given 1.
  Prepare wide gate sauce counters given the sample gate index.
  If the wide calendar example's calculation count is not "1",
    put "Wide gate source calculation count failed case 4." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's requested count is not "2000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000001",
    put "Wide gate source requested count failed case 4." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day distance is not "1000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000001",
    put "Wide gate source distance failed case 4." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day sum is not "2000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000002",
    put "Wide gate source sum failed case 4." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day direction is not 3,
    put "Wide gate source direction failed case 4." into the check report; exit.

To check invalid zero gate indices:
  Put "0" into the sample gate magnitude.
  Set the sample gate index from the sample gate magnitude given -1.
  Put 999 into the gate inquiry's interval length.
  Calculate extended gate spacing for the sample gate index.
  If the gate inquiry's interval length is not 0,
    put "A signed-wide gate index zero was treated as a gap." into the check report; exit.
  Calculate native gate spacing given 0.
  If the gate inquiry's interval length is not 0,
    put "A native gate index zero was treated as a gap." into the check report; exit.
  Calculate native gate spacing given 400000001.
  If the gate inquiry's interval length is not 0,
    put "An unsafe positive native gate index was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Calculate native gate spacing given -400000001.
  If the gate inquiry's interval length is not 0,
    put "An unsafe negative native gate index was accepted." into the check report; exit.

\ Optional SLOW integration: compare completed signed-wide gate
\ sauce against the canonical positive and negative first intervals.
To check wide gate interval positive one:
  Put "1" into the sample gate magnitude.
  Set the sample gate index from the sample gate magnitude given 1.
  Calculate extended gate spacing for the sample gate index.
  If the gate inquiry's interval length is not 345,
    put "The complete wide positive gate interval should be 345." into the check report; exit.

To check wide gate interval negative one:
  Put "1" into the sample gate magnitude.
  Set the sample gate index from the sample gate magnitude given -1.
  Calculate extended gate spacing for the sample gate index.
  If the gate inquiry's interval length is not 503,
    put "The complete wide negative gate interval should be 503." into the check report; exit.
